      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T00:08:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fair point. But I think adding a new apex to DISABLE_ENFORCE_APEX_AVAILABILITY_NAMESPACE_LIST would become a yet-another step for most vendor apexes. \n\n\u003e  Having two copies of this could freeze the libbinder wire protocol. This is true for a number of other libraries as well.\n\nIMO we\u0027d better have a strict guard to prevent this for those libraries instead of relying on apex_available. Like you did in libbinder.\n\nSome nits below:\n\n\u003e e.g. some libraries like libsqlite dealing with FDs assume a process-level lock.\n\nlibsqlite is now available to the virt apex: aosp/2968594. \n\n\u003e  \u0027updatable: true\u0027\n\nThis property is exclusive for mainline modules.",
      "parentUuid": "05fc722c_68b77a70",
